  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Washington has received $13.7B in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The state registered 87,772 awards, with an average award size of $156K. Obligations are down 13.2% year over year, and current-year totals are partial because the fiscal year is still in progress. The Department of Defense led buying with $9B in obligations, followed by the Department of Energy with $3.3B. THE BOEING COMPANY is the largest vendor in the state with $5.9B in obligations, and BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE received $1.3B. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $5.9B, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $1.3B. Other notable vendors and industries include HANFORD TANK WASTE OPERATIONS & CLOSURE, LLC with $787M and Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal at $782M. Readers should treat the FY2026 totals as partial because the fiscal year to date figure does not represent a full-year total.",
    "sections": [
