        "heading": "Which agencies are buying the most in Washington?",
        "body": "The Department of Defense obligated $9B in Washington in FY2026 to date. The Department of Energy obligated $3.3B, and the Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $325M. Other top buyers include the Department of Agriculture at $302M and the Department of Homeland Security at $281M."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Who are the top contractors and industries in Washington?",
        "body": "THE BOEING COMPANY received $5.9B in obligations, and BATTELLE MEMORIAL INSTITUTE received $1.3B. Aircraft Manufacturing is the largest industry by obligations at $5.9B, and Research and Development in the Physical, Engineering, and Life Sciences accounted for $1.3B. Hazardous Waste Treatment and Disposal recorded $782M and Remediation Services recorded $610M."
      }
